# This repo deploys to avataragency.ai via Cloudflare Pages — anything committed
# here becomes publicly fetchable. Keep working files and other products out.

# Local tooling / agent config
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# Editor + OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Working copies and backups — never publish these
*.bak
*.new
*.orig
*.tmp
*.prefix-bak-*
*_snippet.css
*_snippet.html
_preview.html

# LiveBrand is a separate product with its own repo (C:\Dev\livebrand-ops).
# Its design system and mockups must not deploy to avataragency.ai.
design/
docs/

# In-progress builders not ready to be public
clients/prototype/
clone-brand-builder.html
clone-brand-builder.js

# Raw generator output — rename and place deliberately before committing
**/Gemini_Generated_Image_*

# Build output for thrivingincollege.org's own Pages project. NEVER commit it.
# The header rule above is the reason: this repo IS avataragency.ai, so a
# committed thrive-launch/functions/api/checkout.js would be fetchable at
# avataragency.ai/thrive-launch/functions/api/checkout.js — the exact
# server-source leak the launch layout was restructured to close (2026-09-14).
# Cloudflare regenerates both directories on every build.
dist/
.wrangler/
# thrive-launch/ itself IS tracked — Cloudflare needs the Root directory to
# exist in git to cd into it — but only the placeholder. Note the /* form:
# "thrive-launch/" would exclude the directory outright and git will not
# re-include a file inside an excluded directory, so the negation below
# would silently do nothing.
thrive-launch/*
!thrive-launch/.gitkeep
